# YOUR config
# config.toml
# ^ Deliberately NOT ignored in this fork. The parent ZoFHub repo is a PRIVATE
# full-machine backup ("nothing is excluded"), and without this file Nebula
# aborts at startup with `ENOENT: config.toml` — so a fresh clone would have a
# fully built Nebula that still can't run. It holds no secrets: sqlite, no
# postgres credentials, marketplace + masqr disabled. Keep the repo private.

# Goofy PNPM problem
~/
